cards.text:
Deficiencies: A → {{c1::xerophthalmia, night blindness}}
B₁ → {{c2::beri beri}}
B₂ → {{c3::cheilosis}}
B₆ → {{c4::convulsions}}
B₁₂ → {{c5::pernicious anaemia}}.

Deficiencies: C → {{c1::scurvy (bleeding gums)}}
D → {{c2::rickets, osteomalacia}}
E → {{c3::fragile RBCs, muscular weakness}}
K → {{c4::increased blood clotting time}}.

Chemical names: B₁ = {{c1::thiamine}}
B₂ = {{c2::riboflavin}}
B₆ = {{c3::pyridoxine}}
C = {{c4::ascorbic acid}}.

Hormone types: steroids = {{c1::estrogens, androgens}}
polypeptides = {{c2::insulin, endorphins}}
amino acid derivatives = {{c3::epinephrine, norepinephrine}}.

